'''Caitken''' was a [[Mon Calamari]] who, along with fellow Mon Calamari [[Shollan]], served as an [[aide]] to [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] in the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. In [[1 BBY]], the trio was present at a meeting on whether or not the [[Alliance High Command]] should authorize an [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] on the [[Planet|world]] of [[Scarif]] to steal the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the [[Galactic Empire]]'s rumored [[superweapon]], the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. When the mission was carried out by a [[Rogue One|rogue group]] of rebels, Caitken, along with Shollan and Raddus, boarded the admiral's [[flagship]], the ''[[Profundity]]'', to join the group at Scarif.

During the ensuing battle, Raddus turned to Caitken, directing him to call up a [[Sphyrna-class Hammerhead corvette|Hammerhead corvette]] in order to take down the [[Shield Gate]] protecting Scarif. Following the gate's destruction, the plans were transmitted to the ''Profundity'' just as the [[Death Star]] arrived over Scarif. As the admiral ordered the retreat of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]], the ''Profundity'' was disabled and destroyed by a [[Devastator|Star Destroyer]], with most of the crew [[Death|perishing]].

==Biography==
===Aide to the admiral===
{{Quote|I say we fight!|Raddus, while standing in front of Caitken|audio=Raddus-Fight.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:White_Calamari.png|thumb|left|250px|Caitken (left) and Shollan (right) at the base on Yavin]]
[[Homeworld|Hailing]] from the [[Temperature|colder]] regions of the [[waterworld]] [[Mon Cala]], Caitken, along with fellow [[Mon Calamari]] [[Shollan]], served as an [[aide]] to [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="UVG" /> Between [[4 BBY]] and [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Date 3BBY">In ''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]'', the report from Caitken and Shollan is set between the [[blockade of Ibaar]] and the [[Mission to Ryloth (Phoenix Squadron)|mission to Ryloth]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' respectively dates to [[4 BBY]] and [[3 BBY]].</ref> he<ref name="GF" /> and Shollan assembled a report on the status of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet's]] [[starship]]s for Raddus, who then forwarded the report to [[Mon Mothma]],<ref name="TRF">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> [[Commander-in-Chief]].<ref name="UVG" /> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date 1BBY" /> Caitken stood next to Raddus during a meeting in the Alliance [[Great Temple|headquarters]] on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]] where the [[Alliance High Command]] discussed data brought to them by the recently enlisted rebel [[Jyn Erso]]. According to Erso, the [[Galactic Empire]] was building a [[planet]] [[Death|killer]] called the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], and the only way to stop it would be to steal the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[battle station]], located on the planet [[Scarif]]. However, as full support from the council was not received, an attack was not authorized.<ref name="Rogue One" />

Nonetheless, Erso and many other [[Rogue One|rogue rebels]] intended to [[Battle of Scarif|steal]] the plans from the [[Scarif system]] without authorization.<ref name="Rogue One" /> With Shollan and Caitken standing by his side, Raddus was informed of the proceedings and agreed with them, ordering that his [[flagship]], the [[MC75 Star Cruiser]] ''[[Profundity]]'', be made ready for departure. Soon after, the Alliance [[fleet]] entered [[hyperspace]] to support Erso and the other rebels at Scarif.<ref name="RO5">[[Rogue One Adaptation 5|''Rogue One Adaptation'' 5]]</ref>

===Battle of Scarif===
{{Quote|Deflector shields down to 50%! We're sustaining heavy damage!''"<br />"''There's no turning back now! We have to press the attack!|Caitken and Raddus|audio=Caitken-Raddus-Deflectors.flac|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
[[File:MonCalamariTrio-RO.png|thumb|right|300px|Shollan, Raddus, and Caitken on the ''Profundity'']]
Caitken and Shollan interacted with their [[computer]]s aboard the ''Profundity'' as the rebel fleet emerged from hyperspace above Scarif. Caitken was sat to Raddus's left while Shollan was sat to Raddus's right as the admiral called out to each [[starfighter]] [[squadron]] with commands on how to proceed. Later amid the battle, Caitken informed the admiral that swarms of enemy [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]]s were approaching. As the [[TIE series|TIEs]] fired upon the ''Profundity'', the aide announced that the flagship's [[deflector shield]]s were sustaining heavy damage and had dropped to fifty percent. Raddus responded that they could not turn back and must press their attack.<ref name="Rogue One" />

The ''Profundity'' then received a call from the rebel [[Bodhi Rook]] from Scarif's surface, explaining that the only way to retrieve the [[Death Star]] plans would be by destroying the [[Shield Gate]] [[orbit]]ing Scarif. Raddus turned to Caitken and told him to call up a [[Sphyrna-class Hammerhead corvette|''Sphyrna''-class Hammerhead corvette]]. The [[corvette]] ''[[Lightmaker]]'' successfully took out the Shield Gate by sending two [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyers]] crashing into the gate, thereby destroying it and allowing the plans to be transmitted to Raddus's [[Star Cruiser]]. The Death Star then emerged from hyperspace, and Shollan and Caitken stood up to look at the superweapon as it fired upon the [[Imperial Center of Military Research|Imperial security complex]] below, where the rebel forces were stranded. After a moment of silence, Raddus ordered all craft to jump to hyperspace; many ships did so successfully, but the ''Profundity'' was disabled by a [[Devastator|Star Destroyer]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> and destroyed,<ref name="TLJ IC-S">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: Incredible Cross-Sections]]''</ref> with Raddus and all his subordinates perishing.<ref name="Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Rebel Alliance}}</ref>

By [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Rebel Files date">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]'' establishes that ''[[The Rebel Files]]'' was buried during [[Hendri Underholt]]'s [[Bombardment of Durkteel|mission]] to [[Durkteel]] on the same [[Standard day|day]] as the [[Battle of Endor]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[4 ABY]]. As the former also states that ''The Rebel Files'' was [[Excavation on Durkteel|rediscovered]] thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the battle, the artifact must have been found in [[34 ABY]].</ref> a copy of the report compiled by Caitken and Shollan was collected by [[archivist]] [[Hendri Underholt]] for the compilation of non-electronic documents known as ''[[The Rebel Files]]''.<ref name="TRF" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Rebel Files date" /> ''The Rebel Files'' were discovered during an [[Excavation on Durkteel|excavation]] on the planet [[Durkteel]]. Admirals [[Gial Ackbar]] and [[Ushos O. Statura]] of the [[Resistance]] made annotations on the report from Caitken and Shollan.<ref name="TRF" />

==Personality and traits==
Caitken was inspired by the tenacity of Raddus, and along with Shollan, he promised to give him his all.<ref name="GF" /> The three were eager to pay the Empire back for what it had done to the Mon Calamari during the [[Invasion of Mon Cala|invasion]] of Mon Cala.<ref name="GF Shollan">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Star Wars Galactic Files|cardname=Shollan|link=https://www.tcdb.com/ViewCard.cfm/sid/170092/cid/11644214/2018-Topps-Star-Wars-Galactic-Files-RO21-Shollan}}</ref> Caitken was an [[Albinism|albino]]<ref name="EW">''[[Entertainment Weekly's Ultimate Guide to Rogue One]]''</ref> Mon Calamari male with [[Color|white]] skin and gray [[eye]]s.<ref name="Rogue One" /> Due to his hailing from the colder regions of Mon Cala, his [[blood]] was said to be especially thick.<ref name="UVG" />

==Skills and abilities==
Caitken was efficient in following Raddus's orders.<ref name="UVG" /> He was highly intelligent and had diplomacy skills, as well as moderate strength, speed, and fighting abilities. He was not [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="GF" />

==Equipment==
Caitken wore a dark, gray [[Clothing|uniform]] with blue sleeves and a black [[belt]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Just like in our world, [people] all come in different shapes, sizes, and colors, the idea was to expand the Calamari race. The other Calamaris in the film, the white ones [Caitken and Shollan] were more closely derived from Ackbar.|Creature designer [[Neal Scanlan]]|<ref name="Moviemaking">''[[The Moviemaking Magic of Star Wars: Creatures & Aliens]]''</ref>}}
[[File:ShollanCaitkenBTS.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Shollan and Caitken on the set of ''Rogue One'']]
Caitken was created for the [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Rogue One" /> released [[December 16]], [[2016]],<ref name="Dec 16">{{SW|url=news/why-we-already-love-jyn-erso|text=Why We Already Love Jyn Erso|nolive=1}}</ref> where he was portrayed by puppeteer [[Aidan Cook]].<ref name="Cook">{{Topps|set=2017 Topps Star Wars: Rogue One Series 2|cardname=Aidan Cook as Caitken|link=https://www.comc.com/Cards/Non-Sports/2017/Topps_Star_Wars_Rogue_One_Series_2_-_Autographs/A-ACO/Aidan_Cook_as_Caitken/12593897}}</ref> He was first identified in the accompanying reference book to the film, ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="UVG" /> Footage of Caitken was first showcased in a reel of ''Rogue One'' footage revealed at [[Celebration Europe (2016)|Celebration Europe]] on [[July 15]] of that year.<ref name="SW">{{SWYouTube|HUb_zpdyDpU|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story - Celebration Reel|sw_url=video/rogue-one-a-star-wars-story-celebration-reel}}</ref> Caitken and Shollan's designs were reminiscent of Mon Calamari [[Admiral]] [[Gial Ackbar]] from the [[1983]] [[original trilogy]] film {{Film|VI}}, albeit in a different color, while Raddus was more unique.<ref name="Moviemaking" />

Caitken's card in [[Topps|The Topps Company's]] ''[[2017 Topps Star Wars: Rogue One Series 2]]'' set<ref name="Cook" /> incorrectly uses<ref name="Rogue One" /> an image of Shollan.<ref name="Cook" /> Additionally, the [[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|novelization]] of ''Rogue One'' by [[Alexander Freed]] mistakenly attributes Caitken's line of "Sir! Enemy fighters coming in!" to Shollan.<ref name="Novel">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref>

